This function is already minimal, so any speedup will be marginal at best. The rewrite reads the `profile` and `profileIndex` members into locals once. That spares the compiler from reloading them after the null check, and it marks the null-profile path as unlikely. Behavior is unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Field::GetNumSubFields(void) const
{
    const auto p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect(p == NULL, 0))
        return 0;
    const auto idx = profileIndex;
    if (idx >= p->numFields)
        return 0;
    return p->fields[idx].numSubFields;
}
```